# Vouch list — maintainers only (bot commits bypass, but manual edits need review)
.github/VOUCHED.td @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners

# Merge enforcement — these paths decide who can merge. They keep an explicit
# owner so the rules below survive the wildcard above being scoped down.
#
# A workflow triggered by pull_request_review runs the pull request's copy of
# the workflow file, not the one on main, so a contributor can rewrite the
# approval gate in the same pull request the gate is meant to block. Requiring
# a code owner here is what closes that: the tampered job still runs and still
# reports green, but the pull request cannot merge without an approval GitHub
# enforces natively.
#
# The whole workflows directory is covered, not just the approval gate, because
# any workflow can claim a required check context or ask for a broader token.
/.github/workflows/ @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/.github/actions/ @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/.github/CODEOWNERS @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/.github/zizmor.yml @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/MAINTAINERS.md @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/tasks/scripts/check_maintainer_approval.py @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
/tasks/scripts/alert_maintainer_change.py @NVIDIA/openshell-codeowners
